    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_7_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "We used the following bibliographic databases to search for relevant articles: PubMed/Medline, POPLINE, EBSCO/CINAHL, BiblioMap, and ISI Web of Science. We reviewed relevant internet sources from the WHO library database and Google Scholar for additional gray literature. ... We conducted the literature search by using appropriate key words, accepted Medical Subject Headings words, and combinations thereof. One search approach involved using broad search terms ( e.g ., mothers OR women OR female OR adolescent OR pregnant women) combined with intervention-specific search terms such as disease names (cardiovascular diseases OR cancer OR respiration disorders OR diabetes) and NCD risk factors (tobacco use OR smoking OR diet OR nutrition OR alcohol).",
